# The tunnel encrypts and decrypts every packet of a session over the tailnet
# with ChaCha20-Poly1305 in plain C, in the one lwIP task. That task is the
# limit of what the tunnel carries: video takes its share first, and the
# terminal, files and clipboard of OS Services get what is left. From flash
# this code runs through the cache, and its speed then depends on where the
# linker puts it. A firmware image that grew by 14 KiB in other libraries
# moved it and made the terminal over the tailnet 8 % slower.
#
# In internal RAM the code runs at one speed, whatever else the image has.
# It is 4.2 KiB: the cipher, the authenticator and the function that joins
# them. The key exchange (x25519, blake2s) runs once per handshake and stays
# in flash.
[mapping:wireguard_tunnel_crypto]
archive: libwireguard_lwip.a
entries:
    chacha20 (noflash_text)
    poly1305-donna (noflash_text)
    chacha20poly1305 (noflash_text)
